{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeWgMcTddedVRXpH92VU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the 8 test statistics to `.../experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/critique/test_stats/`. I ran each one on the observed `responses.csv`: every one returns a finite float in about 10 ms or less, well inside the time limit. I did not run the posterior-predictive harness, so there are no p-values yet. The pipeline produces those.\n\nThe incumbent model, `personal_alternation_ideal`, judges a sequence only by how close its switch rate is to each person's ideal rate. So the statistics look for patterns that switch rate alone can't explain:\n\n| Statistic | What it measures | Observed value |\n|---|---|---|\n| `equal_alt_balance_pref` | On pairs with equal switch rates, how often people pick the sequence with the more even H/T count. The model predicts 0.5. | 0.61 |\n| `balance_coef_given_alt` | How much an uneven H/T count pushes choices, after accounting for switch rate. | 0.092 |\n| `longest_run_coef_given_alt` | How much the longest streak pushes choices, after accounting for switch rate. | −0.17 |\n| `periodic_penalty_given_alt` | How much people avoid regular repeating patterns (e.g. HHTTHHTT), after accounting for switch rate. | 0.082 |\n| `perfect_alternation_choice` | When one sequence is HTHT…, how often people pick it. | 0.63 |\n| `pair_consensus_extremity` | How strongly people agree on each pair, compared with how much the model expects them to agree. | 0.25 |\n| `left_choice_rate` | Overall bias toward choosing Left; the model has no side bias. | 0.518 |\n| `participant_left_rate_sd` | How much individual participants differ in their Left bias. | 0.061 |\n\nThe longest-streak result points the opposite way from what I expected. Read literally, people choose the sequence with the longer streak more often, once switch rate is held fixed. That is a fact about the data, not a coding error, and the harness will show whether the model reproduces it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4288,"cache_read_input_tokens":43151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4288,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c29c03a-6570-46a5-baf9-7c2b7394c926","uuid":"b3f1352d-1b47-4291-9ec6-79281da5befe","timestamp":"2026-10-03T02:26:44.560Z","request_id":"req_011CfeWgMEPY5p5rJFf3wz9M"}
